From c4812a2ab6a0d0c8f66a345ff9155b5b1b3a043b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gabe Hope <15705900+gabehope@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 23:32:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Add lax.cellPairs: sums over neighbors on a uniform
 grid
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A routine (cpu, wasm, webgpu): for each query point, every source point
in the grid cells within `radius` of its cell (sources sorted by cell,
each cell a range), except itself, with one of three pair functions:
d3's many-body force, a many-body force softened at max(d², 1e-3), and
d3's collision. One thread per query loops over its neighbor cells'
ranges, so any number of points may share a cell: heatmaptest's force
layouts use it for the exact near field of their grid (TODO 30.1),
where fixed-shape kernels had to cap the points per cell.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
